14686592,2025-07-16,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Received bad information about your loan,"In XX/XX/XXXX, I applied for a full loan consolidation to take advantage of the Limited PSLF Waiver. My loan servicer at the time of consolidation was Fedloan Servicing. I have the letters from Fedloan showing that all of my loans were to be consolidated into one loan in the amount of {$57000.00} with the interest rate of XXXX. With the PSLF Limited Waiver, my new consolidation loan payment count was to be the same count as my student loan with the highest payment count ( 111 qualifying payments ) which would put me nine payments away from student loan forgiveness. As my consolidation loan was being processed for PSLF, it was announced that MOHELA was taking over as my loan servicer. Somehow, MOHELA made a processing error, and they only consolidated my FFELP loans. As a result, I have 14 loans with all different payment counts. 

